rfc4422.txt, rfc4505.txt, rfc4616.txt, rfc5801.txt, rfc5802.txt, rfc5929.txt, rfc7628.txt, rfc7677.txt, rfc9266.txt
    The texts of the RFCs, https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc<number>.txt, downloaded on 2026-10-26.
    License: IETF Trust Legal Provisions; the examples are data.
    Used: the examples of RFC 4422 appendix A.2 (EXTERNAL), RFC 4505 §4 (ANONYMOUS), RFC 4616 §4 (PLAIN),
    RFC 5802 §5 and RFC 7677 §3 (the SCRAM exchanges, all four messages), RFC 7628 §4.1, §4.3 and §4.4
    (OAUTHBEARER), and the grammar of the server errors of RFC 5802 §7, extracted from the texts by the tests
    (tests/auth/sasl). RFC 5801, RFC 5929 and RFC 9266 define the GS2 header and the channel binding types.
    Known errors: RFC 7628 §4.4 writes "user=" for "a=" in the GS2 header (erratum 8564, reported 2025-09-04);
    the test expects the original to be refused and the corrected text to read.
